/*
:name: fcall_arg_pun_mismatch
:type: error
:error: argument `a` must be named \(`a=...`\) in call to `sub`
*/

// 06-functions.md "Argument naming", exception 2 binds a bare variable only
// when its SOURCE name matches a parameter. `fwd` forwards its own params `x`
// and `y` to `sub(a, b)`: neither name matches, both params are untyped, and
// there are two of them, so no exception applies -- the arguments must be
// named. (The matching counterpart, `sub(b, a)` from a lambda whose params are
// `a` and `b`, is comptime/fcall_arg_pun.prp.)

comb sub(a, b) -> (r) { r = a - b }
comb fwd(x, y) -> (r) {
  r = sub(y, x) // locate_error_here
}
cassert(fwd(x = 5, y = 2) == 3)
